Lab 10 – SVM

This lab applies Support Vector Machines (SVM) on the Iris dataset.

The data was visualized using pairplot and KDE plot.
The dataset was split into training and testing sets.
An SVM model was trained and evaluated using confusion matrix and classification report.
GridSearchCV was used to improve the model.

Result:
The model achieved high accuracy (~97–100%).
Setosa was the most easily separable class.
